{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>The morning grew light and the men were sent.</b> Even though most grain buyers are accustomed to rise at midnight, he did not send them until morning, for he feared that the man he sends to pursue them and search their vessels might be killed, since people are not yet to be found on the roads."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:32.285396088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}